\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Takeaway: score blind first and reveal the reference only to correct demonstrated errors (M1). Of the protocols tested, it is the only one that keeps a reference in the loop, removes the harm when several answers are valid, keeps the benefit when the answer is unique, and does so at every judge scale tested. The price is one extra judge call per candidate.} What to do about a reference answer, by task structure.}}{19}{table.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
